*Secondary hypotheses:** (H2) Any observed advantage persists when the CoT arm is compared against a length-matched \"verbosity\" control that adds the same quota of extra text without task-relevant reasoning \u2014 i.e., the effect is attributable to reasoning *content*, not merely to additional tokens or instruction salience. (H3, exploratory) The effect of CoT varies by task family and difficulty (e.g., larger gains on multi-step knowledge/order-management tasks than on single-step form-fill).\n- **Operational definitions:** *CoT* = model-generated intermediate reasoning text, elicited by a prompt directive placed in a fixed position in the context before each action, distinct from the action itself. *Task-solving ability* = environment-oracle per-task binary success; aggregated as mean success rate over matched instances.\n\n## 2. Benchmark setup \u2014 WorkArena++\n\n- **Environment [ASSUMPTION]:** Official WorkArena++ suite built on **BrowserGym**, driving a ServiceNow-backed application UI via **Playwright**. WorkArena++ extends the WorkArena benchmark (ICLR 2024) with additional/harder task families; run through `browsergym`-style environments exposing tasks as (template, parameter set) pairs. Family taxonomy assumed ~20\u201330 families (e.g., Knowledge, Service Catalog, Order Management, Software, Sales, ...); exact count/taxonomy to be confirmed from the pinned repo at execution time and recorded verbatim.\n- **Agent loop [ASSUMPTION]:** Standard BrowserGym agent scaffold. At each step the model receives (i) the task instruction, (ii) a serialized AOM accessibility tree of the current page, (iii) the action history (truncated window), and emits an action in the agent action space (`click`, `fill`, `select_option`, `type`/`press_enter`, `hover`, `scroll`, `submit`, `goto`, `close`, `go_back`, etc.). **A reasoning/`think` field is assumed available in the action schema (\u00a73/\u00a79); fallback defined below if not.**\n- **Scoring [ASSUMPTION]:** Binary per-episode success from the environment's automated success checker (oracle) verifying ServiceNow state against the goal; for answer/instruction-following families, success is exact-match on the produced answer, judged by the official checker. No human evaluation in the primary loop.\n- **Episodes/caps [ASSUMPTION]:** Max 20 environment steps per episode; 60 s per step; applied identically to all arms. Episodes exceeding the cap count as failures.\n- **Environment provisioning [ASSUMPTION]:** Self-hosted ServiceNow via the official dockerized setup, pinned to a fixed version/commit; instance state reset to a clean baseline before every episode; repo commit SHA, instance version, and any observed UI drift (DOM hash + screenshot) logged per episode for reproducibility.\n\n## 3. Conditions and agent architecture\n\nThree arms (same scaffold, same observation format, same action schema, same model/checkpoint; **the only textual difference across arms is the reasoning-directive block in the system prompt, in a fixed position**):\n\n| Arm | System-prompt directive (diff line) | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A. Baseline (no-CoT)** | *\"Choose the single best next action and output its JSON. Do not write any commentary or explanation.\"* If the scaffold has a reasoning field, it is suppressed/forbidden. | Reference |\n| **B. CoT (free-form)** | *\"Before choosing the action, think step by step: restate the goal, assess what has been done, identify what remains, and justify the best next action; write this reasoning in the reasoning field, then output the action JSON.\"* | Treatment |\n| **C. Length-matched verbosity control** | *\"Before outputting the action, write exactly N tokens of commentary that describes the visible page layout in plain words (no planning, no goal analysis), then output the action JSON.\"* N matched to arm B's realized median reasoning length in tokens. | Confound guard |\n\n- **Pairing/counterbalancing:** Arms share all other prompt text verbatim, prompt position of the directive block, task ordering, and instance ordering. Arm order per instance is randomized (balanced) across instances; a fresh session/episode is used per arm per instance (episodes are independent, so no within-episode contamination).\n- **Fallback (if scaffold exposes no reasoning field):** Arm B emits CoT as ordinary assistant text preceding a JSON action line; Arm C emits the length-matched filler text similarly; baseline emits only the JSON. Preserves the three-arm contrast.\n- **Robustness phrasing:** A **structured plan-then-act** variant of Arm B (explicit \"Plan: <decomposed goal> / State: <progress> / Next: <action>\") is run as a second CoT phrasing on the head model only (\u00a77.4).\n\n## 4. Sample design and power\n\n- **Design:** Paired within-subject design. A stratified sample of **~80 task instances** is drawn from WorkArena++: ~K instances per family (e.g., ~4\u20138 \u00d7 15\u201320 families to reach 80), stratified to cover representative families and difficulty (single-step vs. multi-step). Each instance is parameterized by an RNG seed derived from a **master seed** (e.g., `master_seed = 20261022`; instance seeds = `hash(family, instance_index, arm_order)`) so the identical task configuration is presented to every arm. **Full suite is noted only as a budget-permitting extension**, not part of the primary analysis.\n- **Repeats [ASSUMPTION]:** Primary paired analysis uses 1 episode per (instance, arm) cell under temperature 0 (matched seeds). Up to 3 repeats per cell (head-model arms) are used for variance estimation and determinism checks; \u00a77 states exactly how repeats enter.\n- **Power calculation (design-time, \u03b1=0.05, two-sided, McNemar):** paired-binary sample size `n = [z_{\u03b1/2}\u00b7\u221a\u03c8 + z_{1-\u03b2}\u00b7\u221a(\u03c8\u2212\u03b4\u00b2)]\u00b2 / \u03b4\u00b2`, where \u03c8 = discordant proportion and \u03b4 = marginal success-rate difference. Using baseline SR \u2248 0.40, \u03b4 = 0.10, \u03c8 = 0.15 (CoT flips ~12.5% of tasks, rarely hurts ~2.5%): **n \u2248 116 instances \u2192 80% power**. At the cost-driven default n = 80, power \u2248 0.64 for \u03b4 = 0.10 (\u2248 0.80 for \u03b4 = 0.13). **Decision: default 80 paired instances (~64% power at \u03b4=0.10), extended toward n \u2248 116 as budget allows; power table and \u03c8/\u03b4 assumptions recorded before data collection.** The supplementary mixed-effects model is more efficient under clustering and mitigates the power cost.\n- **Registration:** master seed, instance-subset list, family mapping, and analysis script are frozen (pre-registered) before any rollout.\n\n## 5. Variables and controls\n\n- **Independent variable:** CoT prompting \u2014 3-level arm (baseline / free-form CoT / length-matched filler); ordinal extension (free-form vs. structured) used only in robustness.\n- **Dependent variables:** primary = binary per-episode success; aggregate = mean success rate over matched instances. Secondary = steps-to-completion, invalid-action rate (steps rejected by env/parser), token and USD cost per episode, per-family success rate, exact-match accuracy on answer families.\n- **Fixed controls (all arms):** pinned model + checkpoint snapshot date; temperature 0 (base policy) with matched seeds; max output tokens fixed; identical AOM formatting, context window/truncation, action schema, step cap, and prompt scaffolding; identical retry/timeout policy. **Sampling fallback:** if the API cannot guarantee T=0 determinism, use fixed T \u2248 0.2 with seeded sampling and **3 repeats per cell**, per-cell success aggregated as modal outcome for the primary paired comparison (first repeat per cell for McNemar; repeats drive variance in the mixed-effects model) \u2014 documented contingency, not the default.\n- **Blinding:** The evaluator (oracle) is automated and arm-agnostic; instance set and seeds identical across arms, so no re-sampling can favor one arm.\n\n## 6. Execution protocol\n\n1. Freeze and record: WorkArena++/repo commit, ServiceNow instance version, model ID + snapshot, seeds, subset list, prompts (three arms + structured variant), step caps, analysis script.\n2. Provision self-hosted ServiceNow; sanity-run 2 demo instances per arm to validate the scaffold and parser.\n3. Roll out episodes in randomized order (averaging out time drift), logging per step: full prompt, reasoning/action text, AOM snapshot, env response, DOM hash, latency, token counts.\n4. Reset environment state before each episode; log git SHA + instance version + DOM hash for drift detection.\n5. Store raw logs immutably; run the frozen analysis script.\n\n## 7. Analysis plan\n\n1. **Primary paired comparison (H1):** On the 80 matched instances (1 episode per cell), \u0394SR = SR_B \u2212 SR_A with a bootstrap 95% CI (block bootstrap by family); test with **McNemar's test** (exact or normal-approximation, two-sided, \u03b1=0.05). Effect sizes: Cohen's h for the SR difference and the discordant-pair odds ratio (n_{B-pass,A-fail} / n_{A-pass,B-fail}).\n2. **Pre-registered robustness of primary result:** \u0394SR also reported with per-arm SR over repeats (modal outcome) if the T>0 fallback is triggered; report n, power table, and observed discordance structure (\u03c8).\n3. **Confound guard (H2):** Compare Arm B vs Arm C (and B vs C vs A jointly). Evidence that B's advantage over A remains when B is contrasted with the length-matched control supports the reasoning-specific explanation; a null B-vs-C difference would caution that CoT's benefit is not attributable to extra text alone. Report \u0394 and CI; interpret cautiously given modest power.\n4. **Efficiency & clustering (H3):** Mixed-effects logistic regression \u2014 `success ~ arm + (1 | family) + (1 | instance)` \u2014 reporting the arm fixed-effect OR and 95% CI; per-family SR tables with exact CIs; steps-to-completion via paired Wilcoxon signed-rank (and paired t on log steps), restricted to successful episodes for \"efficiency\" interpretation; invalid-action rate and cost per arm as descriptive comparisons with paired tests.\n5. **Robustness replications:** (a) structured plan-then-act CoT phrasing vs. free-form CoT (same model) \u2014 consistency of \u0394SR; (b) optional second LLM on a reduced 20-instance subset for cross-model generalizability; (c) determinism sanity check (T=0 same cell twice \u2192 identical trajectory); (d) per-family consistency, flagged if gains concentrate in one family.\n6. **Reporting:** per-task outcome matrix (80\u00d73), arm-level SRs with CIs, McNemar table, model output, and full prompt/log provenance. Conclusions on H1 stated conditional on effect size and CI, not only on the point estimate.\n\n## 8. Feasibility and compute budget\n\n- **Cost model [ASSUMPTION]:** ~80 instances \u00d7 3 arms \u00d7 (1\u20133 repeats) \u2248 240\u2013720 episodes; ~5\u201320 steps/episode \u2192 ~2,400\u20137,200 LLM calls; ~5k\u201320k input tokens/step (AOM can be large) \u2192 ~30\u201390M input tokens total on the head model; estimated cost low hundreds\u2013~2k USD depending on model; wall-clock tens of hours on one worker, parallelizable across multiple Playwright workers.\n- **This workspace:** cannot run the experiment (design-only, no network, no packages, no browser/ServiceNow). Execution requires an external environment with the official WorkArena++/BrowserGym stack, a provisioned ServiceNow instance, and the pinned LLM API.\n\n## 9. Assumptions and uncertainties (dedicated section)\n\n**[ASSUMPTION] Benchmark:** official WorkArena++ on BrowserGym/ServiceNow; ~20\u201330 families; instance parameterization from a master seed; environment-oracle success scoring with exact-match for answer families (~29-family taxonomy in WorkArena, extended in WorkArena++) \u2014 exact counts/semantics confirmed from the pinned repo at run time.\n**[ASSUMPTION] Scaffold:** AOM accessibility-tree observation; JSON action space incl. `click/fill/select/type/submit/...`; a reasoning/`think` field available (fallback in \u00a73 if not).\n**[ASSUMPTION] Model/sampling:** pinned API model/checkpoint; temperature-0 determinism achievable (contingency fallback in \u00a75); token/cost budget as estimated.\n**[ASSUMPTION] Environment:** self-hosted ServiceNow, pinned commit, clean reset per episode; drift logged via DOM hash + screenshots; step cap 20.\n**[ASSUMPTION] Statistics:** two-sided \u03b1=0.05; McNemar normal approximation valid at n\u224880+; discordance assumptions (\u03c8\u22480.15, \u03b4\u22480.10) used only for planning power.\n**[UNCERTAINTY]** Exact family list/count and per-family difficulty mix at execution time; whether the scaffold's reasoning field is exposed as assumed; whether T=0 is truly deterministic on the chosen API; realized token cost vs. estimate; extent of cross-task correlation reducing effective sample size (partially absorbed by the mixed-effects model); possible model-internal (non-prompted) reasoning in the baseline arm \u2014 an inherent limitation of \"no-CoT\" as an instruction-level construct, acknowledged and mitigated by the length-matched arm, not fully eliminable.\n\n## 10. Limitations (candid)\n\n- 80 paired instances give \u224864% power at \u03b4=0.10; smaller effects may be missed, and the B-vs-C contrast is underpowered by design.\n- In-prompt CoT cannot fully silence a model's latent reasoning in the baseline; results read as \"explicitly-prompted CoT vs. not,\" not as evidence about the mechanism of deliberation.\n- All benchmark-specific numbers are assumptions pending verification against the pinned WorkArena++ repository at execution time.", "evidence": "Workspace inspection: /workspace contains only task.json (project brief; track.md = \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\"). No source repos, datasets, or related-work files. Environment check: Python 3.14.4; importlib shows browsergym, selenium, playwright, torch, openai, anthropic, numpy, pandas, scipy, statsmodels